  "notes": [
    {
      "title": "Drawing is a parse-time side effect",
      "body": "index.ts draws in `post()` and replaces the node's attributes, so no renderer imports Vega. The dependencies are dynamic imports inside the branch, so a document with no chart never loads them.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/index.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Half the package is one drawing file",
      "body": "draw.ts is 1369 lines (layout, legends, labels, gantt, waterfall) and read.ts 1065; together they are 2.4k of the package's 2.9k lines, the densest code in the repo.",
      "severity": "warn",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/draw.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "The reader is reused for linting",
      "body": "`draw: false` skips only the drawing call: readChart still runs, so comark-linter gets identical diagnostics without the Vega load. That is why the reader is a separate file.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/index.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Colors are literals, then variables",
      "body": "colors.ts writes light-theme hex values into the SVG so it stands alone; styles.ts then swaps each for the matching --comark-* variable, which is how dark mode works without redrawing.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/colors.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Marks need the scene, not the image",
      "body": "Chart marks reuse annotate's Annotation type and are placed from `boxes` the Vega scene walk returns per mark; marks with no box are dropped rather than drawn in a corner.",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/draw.ts"
    },
    {
      "title": "Only HTML gets marks",
      "body": "Vue and React render `Chart` with `innerHTML` and no marks, and the type says so; a mark placed on a chart is silently absent there, which is easy to miss when adding a chart to a non-HTML page.",
      "severity": "warn",
      "path": "packages/charts/src/vue.ts"
    }
  ]
}